<p>Use venv in the same shell to create a virtual environment that uses Python 3.12, and use the source command to activate it:</p>
<figure class="code-block group/code-block relative flex flex-col [&amp;_pre]:min-w-full" data-has-filename="false"><pre class="shiki css-variables" style="background-color:var(--shiki-background);color:var(--shiki-foreground)" tabindex="0" data-language="bash"><code class="grid"><span class="line" data-line="1"><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-comment)"># This path is an example. You can store the virtual environment wherever you want</span></span>
