<p>You’ll also need to add the following lines of code to the top of the <code>settings.py</code> file to load your environment variables and import the <code>getenv</code> function:</p>
<figure class="code-block group/code-block relative flex flex-col [&amp;_pre]:min-w-full" data-has-filename="false"><pre class="shiki css-variables" style="background-color:var(--shiki-background);color:var(--shiki-foreground)" tabindex="0" data-language="bash"><code class="grid"><span class="line" data-line="1"><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-function)">from</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-string)"> os</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-string)"> import</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-string)"> getenv</span></span>
